        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">An employee earning around RM 3,050/month (after EPF) generally owes zero income tax due to the RM 9,000 personal relief and RM 400 tax rebate.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is PCB in Malaysian salary slips?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">PCB (Potongan Cukai Bulanan) is compulsory monthly tax withheld from your salary by your employer and remitted to LHDNM.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How do I claim a tax refund from LHDN?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">Submit your annual Form BE via MyTax e-Filing. If your total PCB deductions exceed your final calculated tax liability, LHDN will refund the excess directly to your bank account.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

